  {
   "id": "bWiV-k2CwV8J",
   "from": "Souvik Banerjee",
   "author": "da2ca011efc9d511",
   "date": "2012-07-31T20:56:18Z",
   "subject": "Re: [RHadoop:#224] Inserting an matrix in HBase",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<span style=\"font-family:verdana,sans-serif\">It works. Thanks a lot.</span><br style=\"font-family:verdana,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana,sans-serif\">Mistake from my side. Missed this completely. Thanks once again for pointing it out.</span><br style=\"font-family:verdana,sans-serif\">\r\n<br style=\"font-family:verdana,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana,sans-serif\">Also I could retrieve from HBase nicely.</span><br style=\"font-family:verdana,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana,sans-serif\">Here is what I am going for. Let me know if there exists better ways.</span><br style=\"font-family:verdana,sans-serif\">\r\n<br style=\"font-family:verdana,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana,sans-serif\">library(rhbase)</span>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<br style=\"font-family:verdana,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana,sans-serif\">mata &lt;- matrix(data = 1, nrow = 10, ncol = 6, byrow = FALSE, dimnames = NULL);</span><br style=\"font-family:verdana,sans-serif\">\r\n"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<span style=\"font-family:verdana,sans-serif\">matb &lt;- matrix(data = 2, nrow = 10, ncol = 6, byrow = FALSE, dimnames = NULL);</span><br style=\"font-family:verdana,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana,sans-serif\">hb.init(host=&quot;10.118.190.65&quot;, port=9090)</span>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<br style=\"font-family:verdana,sans-serif\">\r\n<span style=\"font-family:verdana,sans-serif\">hb.insert(&quot;testmatrix&quot;,list( list(1,c(&quot;name&quot;,&quot;value&quot;),list(&quot;mata&quot;,mata))))</span><br style=\"font-family:verdana,sans-serif\">"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<span style=\"font-family:verdana,sans-serif\">hb.insert(&quot;testmatrix&quot;,list( list(2,c(&quot;name&quot;,&quot;value&quot;),list(&quot;matb&quot;,matb))))</span><br style=\"font-family:verdana,sans-serif\">\r\n<span style=\"font-family:verdana,sans-serif\">rows&lt;-hb.scan(&quot;testmatrix&quot;,start=1,colspec=c(&quot;name&quot;,&quot;value&quot;))</span><br style=\"font-family:verdana,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana,sans-serif\">readval &lt;- rows$get()</span><br style=\"font-family:verdana,sans-serif\">\r\n<br style=\"font-family:verdana,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana,sans-serif\">for ( i in 1:length(readval) ) {</span><br style=\"font-family:verdana,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana,sans-serif\">    # this is to retrieve only the matrix stored one by one</span><br style=\"font-family:verdana,sans-serif\">\r\n<span style=\"font-family:verdana,sans-serif\">    print(readval[[i]][[3]][[2]])</span><br style=\"font-family:verdana,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana,sans-serif\">}</span><br style=\"font-family:verdana,sans-serif\">\r\n<br style=\"font-family:verdana,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana,sans-serif\">Thanks and regards,</span><br style=\"font-family:verdana,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana,sans-serif\">Souvik.</span><br style=\"font-family:verdana,sans-serif\">\r\n<br style=\"font-family:verdana,sans-serif\">\r\n"
    ]
